WHAT SHIPPED (full parity, no stubs/skeleton)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Native Apple-idiomatic DraftRestorePrompt at parity with the web source. Mounted-once transient prompt:
a bottom-left toast card ("Unsaved drafts restored" + count-pluralised body + Review/Dismiss/Close) and
a review modal (web Modal, via tsModal) listing every draft (label||fallback + "Saved {when}") with
per-row Resume / Discard, plus the per-session one-shot dismissal and the cross-tab active-key surfacing
filter. Adds the full P4 leaf-state contract the web lacks (loading / empty / error / stale / offline).

Files (git status confirms ONLY these 10 changed; .xcodeproj + Frameworks/Shared.xcframework are
git-ignored generated/staged artifacts, not committed):
  DraftRestorePrompt.Adapter.swift     pure core: DraftEntry, DraftIndex reducers (surfaced/removing/
                                        reconcile/normalize), formatRelativeTime port, {{token}} interp,
                                        count-plural body, savedAt, resume-route, a11y labels.
  DraftRestorePrompt.Model.swift        @Observable model (P1/S8) + telemetry (P1/S11) + i18n facade
                                        (P1/S10) + connectivity axis + projection + per-session guard.
  DraftRestorePrompt.Seams.swift        DraftRestoreSource protocol + Static (prod) + InMemory (test).
  DraftRestorePrompt.States.swift       loading skeleton / empty / error(retry) chrome.
  DraftRestorePrompt.Views.swift        toast card / review list / row / freshness chip.
  DraftRestorePrompt.swift              public surface View: phase switch + tsModal review + telemetry.
  DraftRestorePrompt.Previews.swift     #Preview per state (DEBUG).
  DraftRestorePrompt.Tests.swift        adapter + projection XCTest.
  DraftRestorePrompt.ModelTests.swift   model XCTest.
  DraftRestorePrompt.strings            P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution.

Data sources bound via P1/S8 seam (NO direct HTTP/storage in the view):
  useTranslation -> DraftRestoreStrings facade (P1/S10).   useNavigate -> onResume(DraftEntry) navigator
  (web navigate(entry.route)); the draftIndex module -> DraftRestoreSource.
Shared components used: @/components/ui -> TSButton, TSCard, TSEmptyState, TSSkeleton, tsModal (Overlays).
Charts/maps: none (matches web source).

i18n keys (every web t() key reproduced + relative-time buckets + P4 leaf chrome; no English literals in
Swift — all via DraftRestoreStrings/NSLocalizedString):
  draft.recovery.promptTitle / .promptBody.one / .promptBody.other / .review / .dismiss / .close /
  .modalTitle / .modalBody / .empty / .fallbackLabel / .savedAt / .resume / .discard /
  .justNow / .minutesAgo / .hoursAgo / .loadingA11y / .emptyMessage / .errorTitle / .retry /
  .live / .stale / .offline / .staleA11y / .offlineA11y

States (every one renders — verified via projection tests + previews): loading (skeleton card),
empty ("No drafts to restore." friendly state — native improvement over web rendering null), error
(QueryError peer + retry), data (toast + review modal), stale/offline (freshness chip + 1-shot
auto-refresh on stale transition). Dismiss collapses the transient prompt (faithful to web returning
null) — a user action, distinct from the data states, all of which render visibly.

Accessibility: toast title+body = one VoiceOver "status" element (web role="status"/aria-live=polite);
Review/Dismiss/Close + per-row Resume/Discard individually focusable with explicit labels ("Resume
{label}"/"Discard {label}"); skeleton labelled; reduce-motion respected via shared components; Dynamic
Type via system fonts (Font.TS). Telemetry: view.opened emitted once with slug "DraftRestorePrompt"
(P1/S11), asserted idempotent in DraftRestorePromptModelLifecycleTests.

